# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Kriko-m website.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0
- **Method**: Used npm to install the package
- **Files Modified**: 
  - `package.json` - Added dependency
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
- **File Modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
  - Added component: `<SpeedInsights />` in the body section alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component

### 3. Implementation Details
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.2.7 with App Router
- **Installation Method**: Followed official Vercel documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- **Integration Pattern**: Used the Next.js App Router specific import (`@vercel/speed-insights/next`)
- **Placement**: Component added to the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`) in the body section

### 4. Verification
- ✅ **Linting**: Passed with no errors
- ✅ **Build**: Completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ **TypeScript**: Compiled without issues
- ✅ **Static Generation**: All 54 pages generated successfully

## Next Steps

To activate Speed Insights:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard under your project settings
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Once deployed and users visit the site, metrics will begin to appear in the Speed Insights dashboard

## Notes

- The SpeedInsights component is placed alongside the existing Analytics component, maintaining consistency with the project's monitoring setup
- The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices with the component placed in the root layout
- No breaking changes were introduced - all existing functionality remains intact
- The package integrates seamlessly with the existing Vercel Analytics already configured in the project
